### Readings used (declared)
1. ARM ⇔ GHOST invariant: cycling is gated on armed, and every disarm clears
   the ghost — so the KeyM-UNARMED legacy path provably always sees ghost -1
   and lands first-free, literally unchanged. (Task BEHAVIOR exact-list pins
   KeyM-unarmed as today's behavior; an unarmed arrow could otherwise steer
   the legacy place — the invariant closes that.)
2. A REFUSED confirm (green/cap/slot) stays ARMED — clearing the aim is
   cancel's job, never a failed confirm's. The "places ONCE then disarms" leg
   is the success shape (probe-pinned: count+1, green -cost EXACTLY, ghost -1;
   a second MouseLeft places nothing).
3. test_mission_stale.py (the W17e gate) ALSO rode press=place — same coupled
   class as the plan's named retargets ("updated to the new flow IN THE SAME
   card"): its clicks now arm + MouseLeft-confirm through the bridge
   (_place_tower); both stale plants keep failing the SAME legs (stale_buttons
   freeze moved to frame 7, the frame the sync leg tests, so red stays on
   "starved while affordable").
4. Retired-claim scope: the ARCHITECTURE family-picker row ("each pick places
   THAT family's T1") is the claim G5 retires — rewritten same commit,
   replace-not-delete; RELEASE_NOTES.md:122 (v1.2 history copy) belongs to the
